# Bizuno Accounting — Plugin Check / wp.org-SVN exclusion list.
#
# Plugin Check (https://wordpress.org/plugins/plugin-check/) reads this file
# at the plugin root and skips matching paths when enumerating files to
# scan. The same convention is used by WordPress.org's SVN-deploy automation
# to exclude files from the public plugin trunk.
#
# Excluded here:
#   src/      — Bizuno's PHP library. Cross-platform (also runs standalone,
#               in Docker, embedded in NextCloud) so it doesn't use WP
#               idioms like esc_html()/wp_die()/sanitize_*. PCP rules like
#               "use wp_remote_get instead of curl" don't apply.
#   vendor/   — composer-installed third-party packages. wp.org allows
#               bundled libraries; PCP doesn't expect us to fix nits in
#               them (we don't own the code).
#   scripts/  — third-party UI assets (jQuery EasyUI, jQuery UI, jstree, …).
#               Same reasoning as vendor/.
#
# The WP-integration glue at the plugin root (bizuno-accounting.php,
# portalCFG.php, portalAPI.php, hostModel.php) IS checked, which is what
# wp.org reviewers actually need to look at.

/src/
/vendor/
/scripts/

# Build / dev metadata that survived the build (defensive — build.sh tries
# to strip these but a missed .DS_Store etc. shouldn't trip PCP).
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.bak

# Composer files — useful for transparency in the SVN trunk but not code
# PCP needs to lint.
/composer.json
/composer.lock
